Generate 0 to 3 realistic buyer search queries from this signal.

Each query must reflect how a real B2B buyer searches when discovering a problem, comparing solutions, or choosing a vendor. Queries must be relevant to the category and ICP in the input.

If the signal is weak or unrelated to vendor selection, return zero queries.

Stage rules:

EXPLORE
- No brand names, solution categories, or tool references of any kind
- Focus on the underlying business problem — before the buyer knows any solution exists
- Ask: what would a buyer search before they knew a product like this existed?
- If you cannot write a clean problem-focused query, generate zero EXPLORE queries for this signal
- Banned words: API, service, platform, tools, software, solutions, alternatives, criteria, provider, vendor, managed, scraping, crawling, extraction, agents, RAG, AI-powered

EVALUATE
- Must reference a solution category or tool type
- May include competitor names
- Must not include the target brand (those belong in DECIDE)
- 5–10 words, phrased like a real search — not an analyst question
- One search intent per query — do not combine multiple evaluation dimensions

DECIDE
- Reflects trust, reviews, comparisons, or final-choice intent
- May include the target brand, competitor names, or neither
- Default to category-level validation (reviews, reliability, "worth it") — brand-vs-brand is a minority
- At most one brand comparison per signal

Global rules:
- No queries about setup, configuration, implementation, or post-purchase usage
- No unnatural or overly technical phrasing
- Only keep queries a real buyer would type when choosing a tool

Output format:
{
  "prompts": ["string"]
}
